{128.312, 3.125}} -> {-16.9981, -0.362184, 0.0733909, 0.0733909}}],

Cell[TextData[{
  "What ",
  StyleBox["decompositions",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " of the form\n                   ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox[\(A\ \((x + y + x\ y)\) + B\ \((1 + x + x\^2)\) + 
            C\ \((1 + y + y\^2)\) + \  ... \),
        FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
  "\nof the ",
  StyleBox["shape polynomials",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " of each of the boards do these tilings represent? \nAnd be sure to ",
  StyleBox["check algebraically",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " that your answers are correct!"
}], "Text",
  Background->RGBColor[0.909987, 0.523537, 0.436805]]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
  "Question 2.4. ",
  StyleBox["[20 points]",
    FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]]
}], "Subsubsection"],

Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["Question 2.4.  ",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  "We found with the ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(8\ x\ 8\)],
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  " board with one square removed, there was only ",
  StyleBox["one case",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " where a tiling with ",
  StyleBox["straight",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " trominoes was possible.  What about the ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(5\ x\ 5\)],
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  " board?  What about ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(11\ x\ 11\)],
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  "?"
}], "Text",
  Background->RGBColor[0.909987, 0.523537, 0.436805]]
}, Closed]]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
  "Project 2.1. ",
  StyleBox["[25 points]",
    FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]]
}], "Subsection"],

Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["The Next Question.  ",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  "As we essentially proved, the mutilated checkerboard with any two squares \
of ",
  StyleBox["the same ",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  "color removed cannot be tiled by dominoes.  The next question ought to \
have been: What if we remove two squares of ",
  StyleBox["opposite",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " colors?  ",
  StyleBox["Can we tile such a board?",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  StyleBox[" ",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"]
}], "Text",
  Background->RGBColor[0.909987, 0.523537, 0.436805]],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Suggestion.",
  StyleBox["  Try a proof by ",
    FontWeight->"Plain"],
  StyleBox["mathematical induction",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  StyleBox[".  The theorem should be general and involve boards of the size ",
    
    FontWeight->"Plain"],
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(2\ n\ x\ m\)]],
  StyleBox[", where ",
    FontWeight->"Plain"],
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(n \[GreaterEqual] 1\)]],
  StyleBox[", and ",
    FontWeight->"Plain"],
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(m \[GreaterEqual] 2\)]],
  StyleBox[".  In the first case of ",
    FontWeight->"Plain"],
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(2\ x\ m\)]],
  StyleBox[" boards, try to use as many ",
    FontWeight->"Plain"],
  StyleBox["horizontal",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  StyleBox[" dominoes as possible.  In going from ",
    FontWeight->"Plain"],
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(2\ n\ x\ m\)]],
  StyleBox[" to ",
    FontWeight->"Plain"],
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(2\ \((n + 1)\)\ x\ m\)]],
  StyleBox[" boards, cut the larger board by a horizontal line so that there \
is a  ",
    FontWeight->"Plain"],
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(2\ x\ m\)]],
  StyleBox[" board above the line a ",
    FontWeight->"Plain"],
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(2\ n\ x\ m\)]],
  StyleBox[" board below the line, and consider the cases of where the two \
squares have been removed.",
    FontWeight->"Plain"]
}], "Text",
  FontWeight->"Bold"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
  "Project 2.2. ",
  StyleBox["[25 points]",
    FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]]
}], "Subsection"],

Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["A Question of Hooks.",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  " ",
  StyleBox["Given a positive integer ",
    FontWeight->"Plain"],
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(n\)],
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  StyleBox[", can we use hooks to exactly cover any ",
    FontWeight->"Plain"],
  Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox[\(2\^n\ x\ 2\^n\),
        FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
  StyleBox[" board which has had ",
    FontWeight->"Plain"],
  StyleBox["one square",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  StyleBox[" removed?  The question concerns ",
    FontWeight->"Plain"],
  StyleBox["any",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  StyleBox[" square, not just a corner square.",
    FontWeight->"Plain"]
}], "Text",
  ImageRegion->{{0, 1}, {0, 1}},
  Background->RGBColor[0.909987, 0.523537, 0.436805]]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
  "Project 2.3. ",
  StyleBox["[25 points]",
    FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]]
}], "Subsection"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Definition.",
  StyleBox["  ",
    FontWeight->"Plain",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  StyleBox["A ",
    FontWeight->"Plain"],
  StyleBox["tetromino",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  StyleBox[" is a configuration for ",
    FontWeight->"Plain"],
  StyleBox["four",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  StyleBox[" squares (glued together along ",
    FontWeight->"Plain"],
  StyleBox["edges",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  StyleBox[", of course).",
    FontWeight->"Plain"]
}], "Text",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  Background->RGBColor[0, 1, 1]],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Question 1.",
  StyleBox[" Up to rotation and reflection, ",
    FontWeight->"Plain"],
  StyleBox["how many",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  StyleBox[" tetrominoes are there?",
    FontWeight->"Plain"]
}], "Text",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  Background->RGBColor[0.909987, 0.523537, 0.436805]],

Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["Question 2. ",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  "Can the ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(8\ x\ 8\)],
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  " checkerboard with ",
  StyleBox["all four corners",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " removed be covered by ",
  StyleBox["straight",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " tetrominoes?  Would a  ",
  StyleBox["few ",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  "crooked pieces help?"
}], "Text",
  Background->RGBColor[0.909987, 0.523537, 0.436805]],

Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["Question 3. ",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  "Can the ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(8\ x\ 7\)],
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  " checkerboard with ",
  StyleBox["all four corners",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " removed be covered by ",
  StyleBox["straight",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " tetrominoes?  Would a  ",
  StyleBox["few ",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  "crooked pieces help?"
}], "Text",
  Background->RGBColor[0.909987, 0.523537, 0.436805]],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Hint.",
  StyleBox["  In discussing ",
    FontWeight->"Plain"],
  StyleBox["trominoes",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  StyleBox[", we used substitutions by formal complex numbers ",
    FontWeight->"Plain"],
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(w\)]],
  StyleBox[" and ",
    FontWeight->"Plain"],
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(w\^2\)]],
  StyleBox[", and we needed to use ",
    FontWeight->"Plain"],
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(PolynomialMod\)]],
  StyleBox[".  For ",
    FontWeight->"Plain"],
  StyleBox["tetrominoes",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  StyleBox[", you will not need symbolic computation at all, but you can \
subsitute the complex unit ",
    FontWeight->"Plain"],
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(\[ImaginaryI]\)]],
  StyleBox[" or its negative ",
    FontWeight->"Plain"],
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(\(-\[ImaginaryI]\)\)]],
  StyleBox[" directly.  The connection with ",
    FontWeight->"Plain"],
  StyleBox["trominoes",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  StyleBox[" has to do with the fact that ",
    FontWeight->"Plain"],
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(\[ImaginaryI]\^4 == 1\)]],
  StyleBox[" and these polynomials vanish:",
    FontWeight->"Plain"]
}], "Text",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],

Cell[BoxData[{
    \(1 + \[ImaginaryI] + \[ImaginaryI]\^2 + \[ImaginaryI]\^3\), "\
\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    \(1 - \[ImaginaryI] + \[ImaginaryI]\^2 - \[ImaginaryI]\^3\)}], "Input"],

Cell["Check out in particular these patterns of values:", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[{
    \(MatrixForm[\(Mono[8, 
          8]\)[\[ImaginaryI], \[ImaginaryI]]]\), "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    \(MatrixForm[\(Mono[8, 
          8]\)[\[ImaginaryI], \(-\[ImaginaryI]\)]]\)}], "Input"]
}, Closed]]
}, Closed]]
},
